 ## Prices (fallback until we have a token)
-With a token, `GET /instanceTypes?region=eu-west-3` gives real prices, so fetch them into `data/leaseweb_catalog.json`.
-Without one, these are the only figures found (third party, not Leaseweb's site):
 
-| Item | Price | Source |
-|---|---|---|
-| `lsw.c6a.large` (2 vCPU / 4 GB) | 34.39 EUR/month | https://www.vpsbenchmarks.com/hosters/leaseweb/plans (updated 2026-11-06) |
-| `lsw.m3.large` (2 vCPU / 7 GB) | 29.44 EUR/month | same |
-| compute family | USD 14.29-18.12 per vCPU/month | same |
-| general purpose family | USD 17.58-22.38 per vCPU/month | same |
-| traffic | 1 TB/month pooled free, then 2.20 EUR/TB (1-15 TB); incoming free | same |
-| object storage | 0.017 EUR/GB/month, minimum 500 GB | same |
+The project targets the **older** Public Cloud REST API and Terraform provider.
+The authenticated `GET /instanceTypes?region=eu-west-3` response is authoritative
+for that account, region and billing contract, and overrides all local fallback
+prices when saved to `data/leaseweb_catalog.json`.
 
-Load balancer prices weren't found. Leaseweb's own pricing pages are JS-rendered and can't be fetched.
-Pitch angle: AWS egress is about USD 0.09/GB, and Leaseweb includes 1 TB. Put traffic in the cost comparison, because that's where Leaseweb wins, and small instances (smallest is 2 vCPU) are where it loses.
+Without an API token, `data/leaseweb_public_prices.json` contains a dated,
+sourced snapshot of public website prices:
+
+| Example SKU | EUR/month | Website platform | How the report labels it |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `lsw.m6a.large` | 34.68 | New Public Cloud (OpenStack) | Estimated `*` |
+| `lsw.c6a.large` | 30.35 | New Public Cloud (OpenStack) | Estimated `*` |
+| `lsw.r6a.large` | 43.36 | New Public Cloud (OpenStack) | Estimated `*` |
+| `lsw.g6.xlarge` | 253.40 | Older Public Cloud | Published list price |
+
+Sources checked 2026-11-20:
+- New OpenStack Public Cloud: https://www.leaseweb.com/en/products-services/cloud/public-cloud-openstack/pricing
+- Older Public Cloud GPU list: https://www.leaseweb.com/products-services/cloud/public-cloud/pricing
+
+**Platform mismatch warning:** matching SKU names on the new OpenStack cloud
+do not establish prices for the older Public Cloud REST API. Its public
+monthly prices assume a 1-month savings plan and Netherlands availability;
+do not present these proxies as quotes. Public list prices can also differ by
+region, contract, discounts and taxes. If neither public nor API prices are
+available, the existing vCPU-based fallback remains an estimate. The older
+third-party observed `lsw.m3.large` price (€29.44/month) also stays estimated.
+
+Official website networking and storage examples are useful for reporting,
+but **not currently included in the translator's compute cost total**:
+- Older Public Cloud: 1 TB pooled outgoing traffic/month included, then
+  €2.20/TB at the first tier; local NVMe starts at €0.0300/GB/month and
+  network SSD at €0.0800/GB/month.
+- New OpenStack cloud (a different platform): Value block storage
+  €0.0700/GB/month and load balancers €11.02, €22.05, €44.17/month.
+  Those rates must not be silently added to older-platform cost totals.
+
+The report's total is a **priced compute subtotal**, not a complete invoice.
+Verify exact regional pricing, storage, traffic and load balancers before
+making customer-facing savings claims.
